  "id": "Compound::DB00709 - Gene::9356",
  "verbalization": "Lamivudine, a nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitor, is associated with Slc22a6 through a shared pathway involving nucleoside analogs. The evidence suggests that Lamivudine, as part of the broader class of nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitors, binds to Slc22a6 through a common ancestor relationship with other nucleoside analogs such as Stavudine, Didanosine, and Zidovudine. These compounds all fall under the category of nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitors and are known to interact with Slc22a6, a transporter involved in drug efflux and uptake. The presence of multiple pathways linking Lamivudine to Slc22a6 through different nucleoside analogs indicates a potential mechanism of action involving transporter-mediated drug resistance or uptake. The evidence is consistent across different pathways, suggesting a general relationship between Lamivudine and Slc22a6, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
